\subsection{Cross-Judge Replication: Qwen3-32B}
\label{sec:cross_judge}

Qwen3-32B replicates the Blindspot: BT 66.5\% ($[58.5\%, 73.9\%]$, $p < 0.0001$) while Likert $d = 0.011$ ($p = 0.908$).
The higher estimate may partly reflect evaluator-producer bias (Qwen3-32B serves as both rewriter and judge; cross-rewriter validation in Appendix~\ref{app:rewriter_indep}).
Verbosity ORs are highly consistent across judges ($11.34$ vs.\ $13.10$; Table~\ref{tab:gee}).

