\subsection{Cross-Judge Replication}
\label{sec:cross_judge}

Two independent judges replicate the Blindspot: Qwen3-32B (BT 66.5\%, $p < 0.0001$; Likert $d = 0.011$, $p = 0.908$) and Llama-3.3-70B (BT 69.5\%, $p = 0.0001$; Likert $d = 0.010$, $p = 0.846$).
The three target judges span independent architectures (proprietary API, open-weight 32B, open-weight 70B), ruling out architecture-specific artifacts.
Qwen3-32B's higher GEE estimate may partly reflect evaluator-producer bias (it serves as both rewriter and judge; Appendix~\ref{app:rewriter_indep}).

